# config/scheduler-crontab — busybox crond's root crontab, baked into
# Dockerfile.scheduler at /etc/crontabs/root. Standard 5-field cron syntax;
# times are UTC unless the scheduler container's TZ env var is set (the
# image installs tzdata so that actually takes effect).
#
# Each line calls run-job.sh with the exact APP_MODE cmd/api/main.go's own
# switch statement already handles — this file only decides *when*, all
# the actual job logic already existed and was already tested before this
# file did anything. See run-job.sh's own comment for why it's a wrapper
# instead of calling /payroll-app directly.
#
# NOT scheduled here: collect-d2c-debits. main.go's own case for it refuses
# to run at all unless MOCK_MODE=true — there is no real banklink debit
# provider wired yet (see internal/integrations/banklink's package doc) —
# and D2CHandler.Signup independently refuses new D2C signups under the
# same condition, so there is nothing for this to collect against outside
# MOCK_MODE anyway. Scheduling it here would just log.Fatal on every single
# run in production. Add a line for it once a real banklink.DebitProvider
# replaces banklink.NewMock() in routes.go — at that point this is a
# one-line addition, not a redesign.

# Reconciliation — hourly, five minutes past, so it never lands on exactly
# :00 alongside whatever else in the stack schedules on the hour. Tight
# enough that a real drift (a debit that succeeded on Monnify's side but
# never got recorded, or vice versa) surfaces within the hour rather than
# accumulating unnoticed; RECONCILIATION_DRIFT_THRESHOLD_KOBO (defaults to
# ₦1,000, see .env.example) is what keeps ordinary rounding from paging
# anyone at this frequency.
5 * * * * /run-job.sh reconcile

# SOC 2 evidence collection — daily, 02:15 UTC. Collects for *yesterday*
# (see main.go's own comment on this case), so any hour after midnight
# anywhere the org actually operates is fine; 02:15 just keeps it off the
# top of the hour and out of the way of the two jobs below.
15 2 * * * /run-job.sh collect-evidence

# Accrual snapshots — daily, 17:30 UTC (18:30 WAT — Nigeria, this app's
# primary market, is UTC+1). Deliberately late in the business day, not
# early morning: main.go's own comment is explicit that the point is to
# freeze what an eligibility decision *made that day* was actually based
# on, before anything about the employee can change under it overnight —
# an early-morning run would snapshot a day that had barely started.
# Adjust if this deployment's employers mostly aren't on Lagos time.
30 17 * * * /run-job.sh snapshot-accruals
